# Brand colors

Use only this palette. Hex values live in `globals.css` as CSS variables — **never** put raw hexes in `className` (no `text-[#222222]`, `bg-[#ffc527]`, etc.).

| Hex | Token | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `#ffc527` | `primary` | Primary buttons; headings on dark backgrounds |
| `#222222` | `heading` (text) / `primary-foreground` (dark surfaces) | Heading text on light backgrounds; dark section backgrounds |
| `#434343` | `foreground` | Paragraph / body text on light backgrounds |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — random accent, or raw brand hexes in className
<button className="bg-blue-600">Get a quote</button>
<button className="bg-[#ffc527] text-[#222222]">Get a quote</button>
<footer className="bg-[#222222]">
  <h2 className="text-[#ffc527]">Our services</h2>
</footer>

// ✅ GOOD — theme tokens only
<button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Get a quote</button>
<footer className="bg-primary-foreground">
  <h2 className="text-primary">Our services</h2>
  <p className="text-white/80">We renovate villas and flats.</p>
</footer>
```

Prefer semantic usage:

- Page / section titles: use the shared `Heading` (or `PageTitle`) component — it already applies `text-heading`
- Raw `h1`–`h6`: inherit `text-heading` from the base layer in `globals.css`; do not restate the color
- Body copy: inherit `text-foreground` from `body`; use `text-muted-foreground` for secondary notes
- Do not invent a second palette

# Fonts

Use **two typefaces** (heading vs body/UI). Do not ship the finished site on a single family. Family names are TBD — do not invent them. Starter Geist is a placeholder until named.
